From 56e301593d8b3abe1fecf367c389d383fce069b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:56:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(verify): a raw-stock-only mark dies with the model it
 was given to

Second review of PR #1097: the mark named its source by name, so a
model imported under a deleted casting's name inherited it and a real
gouge posted. DeleteEntity (of the source or the stock), UpdateModel
(re-import in place) and SetStock (any new stock) now drop the mark in
their own undo step, and undo restores model and mark together; the
loader reads a mark whose source is missing as unmarked with a note.
An empty model no longer counts as something to judge, and the gouge
hint says what the setting means, shown only for a gouge inside a
stock source no operation names.

Fixes #1094

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
